sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User (student1)
    participant SPA as SinglePageApp
    participant Auth as Authorization Server
    participant IDP as Identity Provider

    User->>SPA: Requests login page (username: student1)
    SPA->>User: Displays login form
    User->>SPA: Submits credentials (username: student1, password: Student)
    SPA->>Auth: Sends authorization request with code_challenge
    Auth->>IDP: Redirects to identity provider
    IDP->>User: Prompts for authentication (login page)
    User->>IDP: Submits credentials
    IDP->>Auth: Redirects back with authorization code
    Auth->>SPA: Returns authorization code
    SPA->>Auth: Sends authorization code with code_verifier
    Auth->>SPA: Returns access token (and ID token)
    SPA->>User: Grants access to the application (logged in)

    Note right of SPA: The code_challenge and code_verifier are used to prevent attacks, ensuring the request is legitimate.
